== The parser at work ==
'N' means {"verb": go, "noun": north}
'Get the Key' means {"verb": tak, "noun": key}
'n' an' 'go north' are the same command: aye
'tak key' an' 'tak lamp' are the same command: nae

== The Bothy at Glen Haar ==

> look
[The Drove Road]
A muddy track winds through the heather. A bothy squats tae the north; a loch glints tae the east.
Ye see: map
Exits: east, north

> status
Naething's been done in the glen yet.

> Get the MAP
Ye tak the map.

> e
[Loch Haar]
Black water laps at the stanes. The wind is fair snell.
Ye see: key
Exits: west

> take key
Ye tak the key.

> go west
[The Drove Road]
Exits: east, north

> dance a reel
Ah dinnae ken how tae 'dance'.

> n
[The Bothy]
A stane bothy wi' a cauld hearth. A ladder climbs tae a loft, an' there's a hatch in the flair.
Ye see: matches
Exits: down, south, up

> down
The hatch is locked ticht.

> tak matches
Ye tak the matches.

> u
[The Loft]
Dusty rafters an' auld sacks. Somebody's left their gear.
Ye see: lamp, sack
Exits: down

> grab lamp
Ye tak the lamp.

> tak sack
The sack is fu' o' tatties. Ye leave it be.

> d
[The Bothy]
Exits: down, south, up

> use key
The key turns wi' a skreich. The hatch is open.

> d
[The Cellar]
It's pit-mirk. Ye cannae see a thing.

> tak quaich
Ye're fummlin' aboot in the dark.

> use matches
Ye licht the lamp. The matches are aw done.

> look
[The Cellar]
A wee stane cellar. In the corner, on a barrel, sits a siller quaich.
Ye see: quaich
Exits: up

> tak quaich
Ye tak the quaich.

> tak haggis
There's nae haggis here.

> inventory
Ye're cairryin': KEY, LAMP, MAP, QUAICH

> drop map
Ye drap the map.

> 
Eh? Say something.

> status
  hatch: open
  lamp: lit

> up
[The Bothy]
Exits: down, south, up

> s
[The Drove Road]
Exits: east, north
Ye step oot ontae the drove road wi' the siller quaich. Slainte!

== The reckoning ==
Commands played: 27 o' 27; moves: 8
Rooms visited: 5 o' 5
Pack holds exactly the key, lamp an' quaich: aye
Rooms wi' something left in them: [cellar, loft]
The day went as planned: aye
